{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "12", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "49", "S": "17"}}, "news": [{"title": "Ghaziabad civic body slashes property tax for small shops", "para": "In a significant relief for small shop owners, the Ghaziabad Municipal Corporation has slashed property tax rates for establishments up to 120 sq ft to 1.5 times the residential rate. This beneficial change is set to aid over 30,000 traders in the city. Additionally, a one-time settlement scheme launching on August 15 will remove penalties and late fees, addressing a long-standing request from the trader community.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/retail/ghaziabad-civic-body-slashes-property-tax-for-small-shops/133173129?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-52162/133173129.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "retail"}, {"title": "Land supply, urban planning reforms critical for affordable housing: NITI Aayog's Rajiv Gauba", "para": "Land supply and urban planning reforms are critical for affordable housing expansion. States and municipal authorities must unlock land and ease development norms. NITI Aayog proposes expanding planned urban areas and reserving land for affordable housing. Access to capital and strengthening rental housing ecosystems are also key. Government entities should unlock unutilised land for housing projects.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/land-supply-urban-planning-reforms-critical-for-affordable-housing-niti-aayogs-rajiv-gauba/133173083?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-40354/133173083.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Bhubaneswar civic & development bodies raze 330 transit houses in joint drive", "para": "Authorities demolished 330 temporary shelters in Bhubaneswar on Tuesday.  Residents had overstayed in these transit houses, which were meant for temporary housing.  Many beneficiaries were allotted permanent homes but continued occupying the shelters.  The Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation and Development Authority conducted the eviction drive.  Further demolitions are planned for Wednesday to clear remaining transit homes.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/bhubaneswar-civic-development-bodies-raze-330-transit-houses-in-joint-drive/133173040?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-165318/133173040.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}